kind: graph
semantic_diff: >-
  Three evidence-strength changes in one graph revision: an acceptance instrument
  must be shown to fail before it grades anything, a zero-hit scan must state what
  it scanned, and a refusal that closes a campaign must rest on a measurement.
  Counts: 32 nodes / 95 edges / 15 checks become 32 / 95 / 16; 5 control endpoints
  and 24 evidence definitions unchanged. No node, outcome, edge, or evidence
  definition is added or removed, and no check is dropped or weakened. Field
  evidence is the verified learning set of a finished port campaign of the
  retiring sibling workflow (vllm-neuron-model-port, DeepSeek-V4-Flash on a
  trn2.48xlarge) re-checked at Neuron SDK 2.32 and vllm-neuron 0.24: the same
  hardware class and stack as a parity run, but not a parity run. Every learning
  cited below is in the Carry set (three filters, two refuters) and was audited
  block against source; the four ids named here are L-204, L-119, L-139 with
  L-082, and L-140, and their persistence verdicts were read from the primary
  persist files, not from the record's summary lines.
  (1) INSTRUMENT LIVENESS BEFORE ACCEPTANCE. preregister_acceptance registers, per
  criterion and as adjudicable values, an instrument-liveness pair: the value that
  must appear as evaluated in the evidence, and a tripwire input the procedure must
  fail on. realize_measurement_procedures feeds that tripwire in the smoke run it
  already performs and records the procedure failing on it. The existing check
  procedures_smoke_verified now asks for that negative control beside the passing
  smoke, so no check is added there. stabilize_and_package_evidence records, per
  criterion in each bundle, the threshold evaluated with the value read and the
  comparison result, plus the procedure's negative-control result; bundles_stable
  and collection_defect_found say so, and an empty evaluated-threshold record is an
  incomplete bundle on the route it already has. One new check,
  acceptance_threshold_evaluated (mechanical, evaluated by the lead), rides the
  existing edge measurements_to_adjudication beside the two lead-mechanical checks
  already on it, and fails back to stabilize_and_package_evidence. A criterion whose
  instrument cannot be made to fail takes the existing criteria_unadjudicable
  outcome down the existing edge to re-derivation: no outcome and no edge is
  invented. WHY, generally: acceptance here is a comparator's word, and the field
  evidence found a shipped parity comparator that returns exit 0 with an empty
  evaluated-threshold list whenever the criterion it needed was not recorded, and
  hard-fails on any divergence when it was (L-204, persists_verified against the
  script itself; the construct reads JSON captures and imports none of the stack,
  so no SDK or plugin upgrade can move it), and a sealed pre-registered gate that
  hard-coded the changed value at a lower level, never executed the code the fix
  changed, and graded a correct fix FAIL (L-119, persists_verified: the knob is
  still a plain kwarg with no env or CLI exposure at 0.24). Both are one defect: the
  graph believed an instrument nobody had ever seen fail. This is the acceptance
  ladder's own guard (pave-spec 5.3.1 - a metric that does not measure the
  acceptance property is as much a defect as missing evidence) against the smell
  acceptance by assertion (13). It holds for any run because it names no
  comparator, no metric and no tool: it asks the instrument to demonstrate that it
  can fail, and asks the evidence to show which threshold it actually evaluated.
  (2) A ZERO-HIT SCAN STATES WHAT IT SCANNED. record_changeset's two mechanical
  scans (the NxDI import scan, P4, and the substrate-fidelity check, P13) carry the
  scan-completeness discipline pinned once at references/artifact-layout.md section
  4.6, beside the exit-code discipline already there: the commit scanned, the tree
  state it was scanned in, and the scan tool's own completion signal. The graph
  states the duty and cites the shape; the shape and its mechanics (a fresh
  checkout at the commit under test for a tool that gates on tree cleanliness)
  land in the reference with the plugin release, so this hunk and that release
  belong to one landing. WHY, generally: a scan whose validity gates on a clean
  tree reported an invalid scan because untracked bytecode directories made a
  long-lived checkout dirty (L-139), and a truncated dump gave a false grep-zero
  (L-082, whose audited corrected rule is completion marker, size stable across
  two reads, checksum, well-formed tail). A zero nobody can show complete is not
  evidence, and it fails both ways: a false hit costs a rescoping lap, a false
  zero sends a forbidden import to hardware under a green changeset.
  (3) A REFUSAL THAT CLOSES A CAMPAIGN RESTS ON A MEASUREMENT.
  acquire_hardware_lease.no_host_available gains required_evidence
  (hardware_attempt_log) and states that each per-host refusal names the measured
  state it rests on, and that a precheck clause no host of the class can satisfy is
  a defect in the precheck, recorded and re-run, never a refusal. WHY, generally:
  this outcome's only edge is lost_hardware_to_closeout into close_campaign, so it
  closes work the user approved, and it carried no required evidence at all, which
  put a campaign closure below the evidence ladder on a doer's self-report
  (pave-spec 5.3.1). The field evidence is a readiness precheck whose clause could
  never pass on that hardware class and refused four devices that direct
  measurement then showed present and free (L-140; its Rule field is narrative, so
  the instruction written here is mine and the mechanism is the reason).
  PRICE PER RUN: no new seat, no new node, no new lap, no new artifact file. Item 1
  costs one extra invocation per declared procedure inside the smoke run that
  already happens, one lead-run read per evidence bundle at the gate into
  adjudication, and one registered line per criterion. Item 2 costs one fresh
  checkout per changeset scan, seconds. Item 3 costs one probe output per refused
  host, on a path that runs only when no lease can be had. Against that, item 1 is
  the only guard the graph has against a false parity PASS becoming an
  evidence-backed pull request, which is the most expensive defect this workflow
  can produce.
  WHAT WAS CUT, AND WHAT WAS REJECTED. Nothing is deleted from the graph; the
  diff is 63 added lines against 12 rewritten, a net 51 lines of graph text. The
  release patch that accompanies this revision is a net ADDITION, not a cut: 25
  files, 970 added lines against 103 removed, a net 867, of which the four
  references take 518 added against 4 removed, a net 514. It carries one new
  reference of 372 lines citing 96 verified learnings that no existing
  reference's reader could reach, priced and justified in VERSION 1.5.0. Across
  both layers all 172 carried learnings are cited, none uncited - 171 by id in
  the release layer's references and 6 here - and that figure is citation
  coverage, not duty coverage. The 172 ids collapse to 29 rules in the release
  layer, beside the 3 duties here, 32 across both layers; the basis for 29 is
  greppable, 13 Rule blocks in toolchain-evidence-pitfalls.md, 8 added Rule
  lines in measurement-pitfalls.md (12 to 20), 4 named duty blocks in
  artifact-layout.md, 3 items in the new section of
  patch-mechanism-inventory.md, and 1 new refusal class in the compile-cache
  guard. One mechanism gets one rule and every id that found it. What pays for
  the growth inside the package: a 25-line restatement cut from the lead skill
  to a 13-line pointer, no duty text restated in any seat contract, one
  reference left untouched on purpose, and a new document-ceiling test that pins
  every prose file in the package so the next release cannot grow one silently. Rejected as prose, not graph, after
  the section-2.1 layer test: the 17 learnings the digest proposed for
  execute_attempt_loop and the 8 for realize_increment are triage procedures and
  coding rules (how to read a watchdog timeout back to the first device fault, how
  to bound a clamp, which flags are inert), so they change no outcome, no evidence
  and no route; the venv learnings are probe mechanics already settled by the three
  self-verification probes the node declares (a co-tenant package tree fails the
  existing sentinel round-trip probe, so a fourth probe would be a second gate on
  one claim, which pave-spec 4.11 forbids); the compile-bucket costing and
  release-note learnings sharpen an investigator's method, not the graph's
  evidence. Rejected as a graph edit for one incident: a named int64-clamp census
  (L-280) is not in the graph, because a graph that lists today's dtype hazard by
  name is a patch; the durable clause is item 2 plus the design record's existing
  per-increment acceptance declaration, and the census itself lands in the release
  layer where a reader can re-derive it at the next pin.
  USAGE EVIDENCE (rule 8). No usage record of a predecessor parity run is reachable
  on this host, so the recorded field evidence read instead was this root's VERSION
  entries 1.2.0 through 1.4.0 and the semantic diffs of revisions 1 through 4. They
  changed this proposal: every one of those four revisions cut priced judgment that
  never fired (17 screen laps on an unmoved pin, 19 preregistration laps on a
  never-opened registration, 51 scoping laps whose priced outcome never fired) and
  the one revision that added a seat added twenty to fifty-five of them per
  campaign, so this proposal adds no seat and puts all three items on the
  lead-mechanical rung, where the answer is a read of a persisted artifact. Nothing
  in those records shows a measurement-boundary seat that never fired, so nothing
  here retires one.
envelope_check: changed_with_approval
plan_evidence: verified
usage_evidence: field
changelog_entry: >-
  Revision 5 (graph): an acceptance instrument must be shown to fail before it
  grades anything, a zero-hit scan must state what it scanned, and a refusal that
  closes a campaign must rest on a measurement. Checks go from 15 to 16
  (acceptance_threshold_evaluated, mechanical, lead, on the edge into
  adjudication); nodes and edges stay 32 and 95. preregister_acceptance registers
  a per-criterion liveness pair (the value that must appear evaluated, and a
  tripwire the procedure must fail on), realize_measurement_procedures proves it
  in the smoke run it already does, procedures_smoke_verified asks for that
  negative control, and each evidence bundle carries the threshold it evaluated
  with the value read. record_changeset's two mechanical scans carry the
  scan-completeness discipline (commit scanned, tree state, completion signal).
  acquire_hardware_lease.no_host_available now requires the attempt log and names
  the measured state behind each refusal. Field evidence, a finished campaign of
  the retiring sibling workflow on the same hardware class re-checked at Neuron
  SDK 2.32 and vllm-neuron 0.24: a shipped parity comparator returns exit 0 with
  zero thresholds evaluated when no threshold was recorded (L-204); a sealed
  pre-registered gate hard-coded the value below the code it claimed to grade and
  failed a correct fix (L-119); a cleanliness-gated scan reported an invalid scan
  over untracked bytecode and a truncated dump gave a false grep-zero (L-139,
  L-082); a readiness precheck clause that no device of that class could satisfy
  refused four devices that measurement showed free (L-140).
